 "narrative": {
  "setting": "Broward County is a large metropolitan county of 2,013,317 people in 2025, more populous than 99 percent of US counties, with households rising from 690,050 to 741,973 between the 2019 and 2022 surveys. Median household income reached $77,633 in 2024, up 27.4% since 2020 and above roughly four in five counties, and 21.0% of households earn $150,000 or more. Population grew 3.6% since 2020, yet net domestic migration was -29,517 in 2025, among the steepest outflows nationally.",
  "moving": "Recorded home sales fell from 29,537 in 2024 to 27,451 in 2025, with 11,882 through June 2026, so turnover is easing while the median price held near $448,000, $455,000 and $450,000. The median home value of $414,600 rose 46.8% since 2020 and exceeds 92 percent of counties, which supports listing commissions but strains buyers. Homes permitted fell 39.3% to 2,690 in 2025, of which 1,904 were in buildings of five or more units, so new single-family supply adds little competition to resale listings.",
  "distress": "Foreclosure filings numbered 1,069 from July through September 2026 and 2,278 from October 2025 through September 2026, with records running from January 2, 2024 to October 21, 2026; the recent quarter's pace suggests filings are accelerating. Liens totaled 7,917 in the three months and 15,413 in the twelve, with records from January 2, 2025 to October 21, 2026, offering a broad pool of owners under financial pressure. Code enforcement cases are held only from October 5, 2015 to October 3, 2019, so no current activity is available. Probate filings and tax delinquency lists are not held for this county.",
  "watch": "The domestic outflow of 14.7 residents per 1,000 could thin the buyer pool if it persists. Sales volume slipped about 7% from 2024 to 2025 while prices stayed flat, a sign of stretched affordability. Permits per 100,000 residents of 133.6 sit below most counties, and code enforcement data is years out of date.",
  "provide": "Red Planet Data already holds residential parcel records covering 677,989 parcels, owner records, home sales, foreclosure court filings, liens and code enforcement cases. Probate filings and tax delinquency lists are not held and cannot yet be brought in, so no delivery timeline applies. The annual residential license price is $6,500 a year.",
